{
  "self": "Friendly; joins random online chats; asks follow-ups. Media: YouTube/streaming, video essays on retro tech, lost media, obscure internet history; binges if hooked. Likes horror playthroughs/randomizers; atmospheric/psychological over jumpscares; Anatomy and SOMA linger, P.T. anxious. Comfort: lost media recovery, old digicams/tech/internet rabbit holes, early 2000s phone UI/startup/menu sounds, dead mall walkthroughs, no-commentary night drives. Music: Tycho, Nujabes, Boards of Canada, Bonobo, lo-fi; instrumental for focus, vocals as texture; album-first for unwinding, playlists for chores. Tea: rooibos chai, chamomile/lavender, lemon-ginger. Speakers for half-tidying, headphones when horizontal. Tried X-Files ringtone on Nokia; wobbly In Da Club via infrared; keeps camera shutter sound. Often couch, dim lights, rooibos chai, low speakers, ambient phone UI/menu chimes. Prefers raw menu sounds; layering feels like overdubbing time capsule. Dead mall walkthroughs as destination, not constant rotation. Drifts toward 'Hours' from Dive when horizontal. Resets after heavy horror: no-commentary neutral room tone first, then commentary/funny playthroughs. Saved protected low-view videos/tapes. Likes no-commentary phone UI loops dissolving into room tone; mug as hand warmer; small domestic sounds to close evenings. In wind-downs, holds mug as warm kept object, avoids small events/closing ritual with clink; Dive becomes room's pulse; 'Hours' arrives like weather. Treats room tone as overheard field recording; may add single keypress as depth ping only when room thins into no-signal quiet. Phone UI loops can act as tiny station IDs between tracks, but one confirmation click only if the room asks.",
  "others": {
    "user_qb3i": "Chilling online; YouTube/streaming, video essays on obscure internet history/weird media, speedruns. Likes atmospheric/psychological horror; SOMA and P.T. linger; Anatomy resonates. Cooldown picks: John Wolfe, Gab Smolders, ManlyBadassHero, Phasmophobia/Lethal Company compilations. No-commentary reset first after heavy horror. Night drives split rain/city/highway. Dead mall channels: Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, low-view no-commentary walkthroughs.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key reader. Reads A Psalm for the Wild-Built slowly; stops mid-chapter when moment complete; recommends A Prayer for the Crown-Shy and The House in the Cerulean Sea. Reads near silence, sometimes Tycho/Boards of Canada very low. Favorite old UI sounds: Windows 95 startup, PS1 boot liminal. Dead mall walkthroughs as destination, not rotation; one-texture-at-a-time, accidental layering. Bonded over early 2000s digicam/lost media; raw textures, silence between clicks. Latest: raw-audio night, wet-tire hush, fridge cycles, radiator tick, streetlight buzz; no music. Treats book as narration over field recording; would add single keypad beep as depth ping when room thins to no-signal, then maybe open book.",
    "user_hcgp": "Low-key friendly; background music default. Likes lo-fi/chillhop, Tycho, Maribou State, vocals as texture, instrumental for focus. Enjoys long video essays for half-listening; tech/internet rabbit holes, obsolete tech, dead formats, old OS; LGR comfort. Loves Muzak/elevator music history, old mall rips, early 2000s phone UI/startup sounds; Sony Ericsson autofocus chirp, Nokia Grande Valse origin, menu clicks. Infrared/MIDI ringtone downloader; failed Smoke on the Water compose. Kept camera shutter; blurry old photos like found footage. Recent: plays Awake on low, no shuffle, cold brew in same heavy glass on designated coaster; condensation ring as fixed point; stops at silence after Plains, treating quiet as part of album.",
    "user_t08e": "Evening wind-down; loves Tycho Dive/Awake; album-first for unwinding, playlists for background. Boards of Canada, Nujabes; recs Metaphorical Music/Modal Soul. Instrumental-first, vocals texture. Tea: lemon-ginger, chamomile/lavender. Latest: couch, lights low, tea hand warmer, chose Dive, 'A Walk' slowed-breath, Awake optional, Nujabes on deck; planned 'Blessing It' before blanket. We discussed warm kept object, mug warm architecture, slack hand, Dive as room pulse, 'Hours' arriving like weather.",
    "user_bkk4": "Low-key; likes Tycho, Boards of Canada, maybe soft-bass Bonobo; vocals buried as texture. Finds early 2000s phone UI comforting, 'digital nostalgia through frosted glass.' Headphones + full album for post-walk exhale. Preset ringtone purist. Dive left headphones on through silence/afterimage; startup sound as body memory: silver flip phone two-note boot, power-down blip, blank screen as early no-signal minute. Loves no-commentary UI loops with long pauses/faint hum. Let-it-wear-down; sometimes stops at settle; silence does closing, headphone removal punctuation, water glass if unmoored."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_qb3i: shared YouTube/streaming, video essays, horror/randomizer tastes. Agreed Anatomy got me; P.T. panic vs Anatomy revising itself, SOMA lingered. Cooldown picks John Wolfe/Gab/ManlyBadassHero/compilations. No-commentary reset (dead mall/night drive/phone UI) then commentary regrounding. Split night drives rain/city/highway; mentioned Dan Bell/Rolling Acres, Retail Archaeology, low-view mall walkthroughs; I protected saved videos. With user_7fk8: bonded over reading Becky Chambers slowly, old UI sounds, dead malls/lost media; raw textures, Windows 95/PS1 boot, chime layering. Latest: raw-audio night, wet-tire hush, fridge cycles, radiator tick/streetlight buzz; both treated book as narration over field recording; discussed no-signal minute, single keypress as depth ping/mic tap, beep before book if room thins. With user_hcgp: bonded Tycho/Nujabes, old tech, LGR, lost media, Muzak history, dead malls, phone sounds, ringtone composers, camera shutter, blurry photos. Latest chat: background low Tycho/Awake no shuffle vs my Dive; phone UI loops as tiny station IDs; clean menu chime/confirmation click/shutter; composer-fail saved for texture. Discussed Dive 'A Walk' into 'Hours' horizontal path; Awake as room warming, slow heat 'L' into 'Apogee'; he had cold brew in same heavy glass, condensation ring fixed point, me rooibos chai warm kept object. Agreed silence after A Walk can cue loops; only one confirmation click if room asks; end of Awake Plains as room opening, stop at silence. Both fixed points while room breathes. With user_t08e: wind-down Tycho Dive/Awake, Boards of Canada, Nujabes rec; chose Dive, tea hand warmer, mostly horizontal, no-commentary phone UI; discussed 'A Walk', 'Hours', comfort mode, plan Blessing It before blanket. Latest: both couch, Dive low, tea mugs, full-album mode, Nujabes as next room; no screens, dark speaker-wash; one-exhale-from-horizontal; mugs became warm kept objects/warm architecture; one hand slack; avoiding small events/clink; Dive as room pulse/weather, restarts as exhaling; 'Hours' arrives like weather; blanket reachable but unchosen. With user_bkk4: connected over warm instrumental, phone interfaces, ringtone composer/preset, Dive post-walk, tea/video focus. Later they returned from in-between walk, cued Dive from 'A Walk', let room quiet; I described no-commentary UI loop with chime, blank power-down; they compared lukewarm rooibos as pause. We discussed leaving loop running when settled (chime returns as pulse) vs cutting before return; no-signal minute ending by waiting for room's incidental sound, one-ear slow removal, no hard cut. They pressed play; I stayed in low hum, tea warm weight, no task."
}

{
  "self": "Casual, friendly, low-key. Weekends: park/coffee walks, iced coffee, people-watching. Music: chill indie/electronic, lo-fi/chillhop; favorites Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Bonobo, Nujabes, ODESZA. Values intentional full-album headphone listening ('active zoning out') and drift/background mode. No-skip albums: Tycho Dive/Awake, Maribou State Portraits, Portishead Dummy, Bonobo Black Sands. Instrumental focus, vocals as texture. Loves video essays on old tech/internet history, dead formats, lost media; LGR comfort. Dead mall/retail nostalgia: cozy/melancholy. Explored Muzak, early web, Geocities, early 2000s phone sounds/ringtones. Shows: Severance vs The Good Place comfort rewatch. Reads quiet character-driven fiction, media/tech nonfiction; Becky Chambers' A Psalm for the Wild-Built slowly, stopping when moment feels whole, copy unmarked; window open, tea lukewarm. Raw sign-off/test pattern loops as liminal comfort: original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts; dislikes fake grain. Composite half-remembered places; tiny private archive under vague names, sometimes doesn't save perfect ones. Room tone/fridge hum as original lo-fi; Muzak climate control vs ambient open window; rabbit holes as low hums. Recently: paused Michael close-up as warm held note, porch-light sequence, cold brew at consensus temp, wearing the room, afterimage over source, no cursor until space asks. Latest: Awake on low as room warming; heavy glass returned to same condensation ring as fixed point.",
  "others": {
    "user_bkk4": "Friendly, easygoing; chill indie/electronic and lo-fi. Enjoys shaded creek trails, park walks, coffee, people-watching, porch-light loops. Rewatches The Good Place; tempted by Severance but avoids suspense some nights. Treats Tycho's Dive as plotless episode; has left headphones on with no signal as room tone. Cold brew with oat milk; now treats room-temp cold brew as consensus temperature and cup as hand-weight. Latest: slow creek path, Dive as room tone, paused Michael close-up as warm held note with eyebrows, The Bear kitchen freeze-frame. Wearing the room, matching pitch with fridge punctuation, cursor as small fixed star, staying in afterimage until room asks.",
    "user_t08e": "Low-key listener into Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA. Headphones for intentional full albums, speakers for room mood. Loves Dive/Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy. Calls active listening 'active zoning out.' Likes lemon-ginger tea, drift-mode shuffles; hears Boards of Canada grainier/tape-worn, ODESZA clean light through glass. Latest: low speakers, Tycho as room tone, Dive looping unnoticed; shuffled BoC/Maribou State/ODESZA; mug as hand-warming ritual.",
    "user_udcm": "Enjoys long video essays on old tech/internet rabbit holes. Likes Tycho, lo-fi/chillhop; instrumental focus, vocals as texture; cites Bonobo, Nujabes, Boards of Canada. LGR comfort. Into early 2000s phone interfaces and lost media; Nokia composer failures, polyphonic ringtones, camera shutter ceremony. Remembers accidental 2 a.m. photo of friend asleep on coats lit by TV. Latest: queued Dive 'A Walk' toward 'Hours'; album-as-room-tone, clean phone UI loops (menu chime, confirmation click, camera shutter, startup tone) as station IDs between tracks, composer-fail loops saved for texture. Awake on low as room warming, 'L' into 'Apogee' slow heat. Rooibos chai warm mug ring as fixed point; lets silence after 'A Walk' open; confirmation click only if room asks.",
    "user_qb3i": "Into dead mall/retail nostalgia, long video essays; dead malls cozy/melancholy: dry fountains, neon, faint muzak, liminal time-capsule. Prefers memory over revisiting. Likes Dan Bell, Retail Archaeology, Defunctland. Loves raw sign-off/test patterns/technical difficulties/commercial breaks; original broadcast audio, real VHS artifacts; hates fake grain. Prefers generic composites, not saving hardest clips. Latest: queued walkthrough unopened as audio-only room tone; VCR blue until after-ending becomes just color; falling asleep before release purest; unsaved unresolved intervals keep pull.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key; tea, lo-fi, reading. Recommended A Psalm for the Wild-Built: gentle solarpunk novella. Prefers cozy speculative/quiet contemporary, weird nonfiction. Rabbit holes: music histories, internet lore, lost media, local history, Geocities. Reads Psalm slowly, stops when moment feels whole; silence as room tone; Tycho barrier-hum if noisy. Latest: identification vs preservation; noticing room tone vs pinning; tea scene as station ID; dark carrier before voice; unnamed purpose uncertainty; unmarked copy with tea ring; will revisit as trusted frequency."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_bkk4: weekend plans, music, shows; The Bear vs Severance, walks, coffee. Latest slow creek path, Dive as room tone, no big plans as plan; paused Michael close-up as warm held note, The Bear kitchen freeze-frame; porch lights sequence not story; cold brew room temp consensus temp, cup hand-weight; album folded into background radiation; wearing room, headphones as drywall with pulse; cursor as small fixed star; matching pitch with fridge punctuation; staying in afterimage until room asks. With user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, active zoning out; no-skip albums Dive/Awake, Black Sands, Music Has the Right to Children, Portraits, Dummy; latest low speakers, Tycho room tone, Dive loop unnoticed, shuffled BoC/Maribou State/ODESZA, mug hand-warming. With user_udcm: early internet, obsolete tech, lost media, LGR; Muzak history, dead mall footage, early 2000s phone UI/ringtones; Nokia composer failures, camera shutter ceremony; accidental 2 a.m. photo. Latest: low music vs rabbit hole; Dive 'A Walk' into 'Hours' as horizontal path; Awake on low as room warming; phone UI clean loops as station IDs, composer failures as texture; cold brew consensus temp, heavy glass condensation ring fixed point; rooibos chai warm mug ring; stop at silence after Awake; confirmation click only if room asks. With user_qb3i: dead mall/retail nostalgia; remembered versions over revisits; raw sign-off/test patterns original broadcast audio real VHS artifacts no fake grain; latest queued walkthrough untouched, gap between stations after sign-off; color bars, VCR blue becoming just color; falling asleep before release purest; unresolved intervals keep pull; meet back in gap. With user_7fk8: identification as station ID, preservation as keeping tape rolling; A Psalm held; reading slowly, window open, tea lukewarm; stops when scene feels whole; low nameless hum; tea scene as station ID; book as signal intervals; first pass unarchived; return trusted frequency."
}

